      "message": "Prove two support products replace four scalar sign graphs\n\nRecover L=q^t and Qt1=q^(t+1) using the signed cap and positive-index request lemmas before assuming either output sign. Their strictly positive weighted sums make two direct quadratic product predicates sufficient to restore all four scalar signs on the unchanged original body.\n\nPublish the complete ordinary argument, all 52 literal rows, four graph records and twelve private occurrence sets, complete power/frame interfaces and fresh-triple witness maps. Root and independent full reviews pass. Seal the unchanged ordinary packet and retain root bindings. No source or quartic is emitted, no projected dimension is inferred, and canonical PDF/TeX and paused Lean work are preserved.",
